>>__ load "simpExtLib";
>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `del_split`

``` hol4
simpExtLib.del_split : string -> simpExtLib.simpset -> simpExtLib.simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Removes local split loopers. `del_split name ss` removes `split name` and
`split_asm name`; a name already beginning with one of those prefixes removes
only that looper. Missing names leave the set unchanged.

Persistent attribute rules are unaffected. Use `ExclX ("split:" ^ name)` for
invocation-local suppression, or `splitLib.exclude_split "Thy.Name"` after
explicit registration for persistent retraction. Local removal requires no
registration.

### Failure

Never fails.

### Example

``` hol4
>>_ val ext_bool_ss = simpExtLib.lift_simpset boolSimps.bool_ss;
>>_ val ss = simpExtLib.add_split (splitLib.type_split_of “:'a option”)
     ext_bool_ss;
>>_ val without_option = simpExtLib.del_split "option$option_CASE" ss;
```

### See also

[`splitLib.exclude_split`](#splitLib.exclude_split),
[`simpExtLib.add_split`](#simpExtLib.add_split),
[`simpExtLib.ExclX`](#simpExtLib.ExclX).
